    "markdown": "![ACL Logo](https://aclanthology.org/images/acl-logo.svg) ACL Anthology ⟨1⟩\n  * About⟨2⟩\n    * Announcements⟨3⟩\n    * Communication channels⟨4⟩\n    * Related work⟨5⟩\n    * Copyright⟨6⟩\n    * * * *\n    * Credits⟨7⟩\n    * Volunteer⟨8⟩\n    * Development⟨9⟩\n    * Feedback⟨10⟩\n  * Using⟨2⟩\n    * Citing papers⟨11⟩\n    * Links in the Anthology⟨12⟩\n    * Data access⟨13⟩\n    * * * *\n    * All FAQs⟨14⟩\n    * * * *\n    * ###### Details\n    * Anthology identifiers⟨15⟩\n    * Names⟨16⟩\n    * ORCID iDs⟨17⟩\n    * DOIs⟨18⟩\n    * Verified authors⟨19⟩\n  * Contributions⟨2⟩\n    * Submissions⟨20⟩\n    * Corrections⟨21⟩\n    * Author pages⟨22⟩\n    * Attachments⟨23⟩\n  * GitHub⟨24⟩\n\n\n## Proceedings of the 13th International Joint Conference on Natural Language Processing and the 3rd Conference of the Asia-Pacific Chapter of the Association for Computational Linguistics: Tutorial Abstract\nYun-Nung (Vivian) Chen⟨25⟩, Sadao Kurohashi⟨26⟩ (Editors)\n* * * \n\nAnthology ID:\n    2023.ijcnlp-tutorials \n\nMonth:\n    November \n\nYear:\n    2023 \n\nAddress:\n    Nusa Dua, Bali \n\nVenues:\n     IJCNLP⟨27⟩ | AACL⟨28⟩ \n\nEvents:\n     The 13th International Joint Conference on Natural Language Processing and The 3rd Conference of the Asia-Pacific Chapter of the Association for Computational Linguisticss⟨29⟩ | The 13th International Joint Conference on Natural Language Processing and The 3rd Conference of the Asia-Pacific Chapter of the Association for Computational Linguisticss⟨30⟩ \n\nSIG:\n\n\nPublisher:\n    Association for Computational Linguistics \n\nURL:\n    <https://aclanthology.org/2023.ijcnlp-tutorials/> \n\nDOI:\n\n\nBib Export formats:\n     BibTeX⟨31⟩ MODS XML⟨32⟩ EndNote⟨33⟩\nBibTeX ⟨31⟩Search⟨34⟩\n* * *\npdf ⟨35⟩bib ⟨36⟩\n**Proceedings of the 13th International Joint Conference on Natural Language Processing and the 3rd Conference of the Asia-Pacific Chapter of the Association for Computational Linguistics: Tutorial Abstract⟨37⟩**  \nYun-Nung (Vivian) Chen⟨25⟩ | Sadao Kurohashi⟨26⟩\npdf ⟨38⟩bib ⟨39⟩\n**Language and Robotics: Toward Building Robots Coexisting with Human Society Using Language Interface⟨40⟩**  \nYutaka Nakamura⟨41⟩ | Shuhei Kurita⟨42⟩ | Koichiro Yoshino⟨43⟩\npdf ⟨44⟩bib ⟨45⟩\n**Current Status of NLP in South East Asia with Insights from Multilingualism and Language Diversity⟨46⟩**  \nAlham Fikri Aji⟨47⟩ | Jessica Zosa Forde⟨48⟩ | Alyssa Marie Loo⟨49⟩ | Lintang Sutawika⟨50⟩ | Skyler Wang⟨51⟩ | Genta Indra Winata⟨52⟩ | Zheng-Xin Yong⟨53⟩ | Ruochen Zhang⟨54⟩ | A. Seza Doğruöz⟨55⟩ | Yin Lin Tan⟨56⟩ | Jan Christian Blaise Cruz⟨57⟩\npdf ⟨58⟩bib ⟨59⟩\n**Practical Tools from Domain Adaptation for Designing Inclusive, Equitable, and Robust Generative AI⟨60⟩**  \nAnthony Sicilia⟨61⟩ | Malihe Alikhani⟨62⟩\npdf ⟨63⟩bib ⟨64⟩\n**Editing Large Language Models⟨65⟩**  \nNingyu Zhang⟨66⟩ | Yunzhi Yao⟨67⟩ | Shumin Deng⟨68⟩\npdf ⟨69⟩bib ⟨70⟩\n**Learning WHO Saying WHAT to WHOM in Multi-Party Conversations⟨71⟩**  \nJia-Chen Gu⟨72⟩ | Zhuosheng Zhang⟨73⟩ | Zhen-Hua Ling⟨74⟩\npdf ⟨75⟩bib ⟨76⟩\n**Developing State-Of-The-Art Massively Multilingual Machine Translation Systems for Related Languages⟨77⟩**  \nJay Gala⟨78⟩ | Pranjal A. Chitale⟨79⟩ | Raj Dabre⟨80⟩\n![Creative Commons License](https://i.creativecommons.org/l/by/4.0/88x31.png)⟨81⟩ ACL materials are Copyright © 1963–2026 ACL; other materials are copyrighted by their respective copyright holders. Materials prior to 2016 here are licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 3.0 International License⟨82⟩. Permission is granted to make copies for the purposes of teaching and research. Materials published in or after 2016 are licensed on a Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License⟨83⟩.\nThe ACL Anthology is managed and built by the ACL Anthology team⟨7⟩ of volunteers.\n_Site last built on 22 July 2026 at 14:46 UTC withcommit 280e4ed⟨84⟩._\n",
